      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RUM AND KIRK (1) improving gelding who finds a more suitable contest today. Placed first up at Grafton, then sent to town with a plugging eighth over 1200m at Eagle Farm. Can take control early and prove hard to run down. KOBI EXPRESS (5) seven-start maiden with his hoof on the till. No excuses here with Palmer's 3kg claim after shouldering the 59kg for a tough on-pace second over 1025m at Grafton. Will roll forward in what looks a two-horse race. PIETIERO (7) failed to come up in her first campaign and returns from a five-month spell. Fitted with the two trials and should go on with it this time in. Each way. FLYING MONARCH (3) Trapeze Artist gelding from an O'Reilly mare on debut for the Peter Sinclair yard. Has impressed in two trials and market moves must be closely monitored.",
